; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Sunburst
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     lines, rotation, remainder, color
; SUMMARY:  Shoots rays out from the center in three lengths and warm colors to make a bright sunburst.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle walks out from the middle and back again, turns a
;   little, and does it again, 90 times. Every third ray is long,
;   the next is medium, the next short, so the rays make a spiky
;   pattern. A big round sun covers the middle.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the lengths in RAYLENGTH or the number of
;   rays in the REPEAT.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FORWARD then BACK: go out and come home again
;   * REMAINDER to take turns between three choices
;   * using one number (REPCOUNT) to pick both a length and a color
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make every fourth ray long by using REMAINDER ... 4.
;   * Use cool colors (blues and greens) for an ice burst.
;   * Make the rays fatter with SETPENSIZE 6.
; ============================================================

; Three ray lengths that take turns: remainder 0, 1, 2.
to raylength :n
  output item 1 + remainder :n 3 [260 190 120]
end

to raycolor :n
  output item 1 + remainder :n 4 [[250 80 40] [255 150 30] [255 210 50] [240 110 60]]
end

to sunburst :rays
  repeat :rays [
    setpencolor raycolor repcount
    forward raylength repcount
    back raylength repcount
    right 360 / :rays
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [40 20 60]
setpensize 4
sunburst 90
; the sun: two big dots, a dark ring and a bright middle
setpensize 130 setpencolor [255 120 30]
dot [0 0]
setpensize 110 setpencolor [255 220 80]
dot [0 0]
